invariant: INV-17
file: sha512_avx2.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha512-avx2
reason: SHA512_AVX2_BELOW_LEN, the bytes of stack sha512_hw.c wipes below
  each call of the AVX2 kernel, is 192, less than the frame
  sha512_avx2_compress_blocks writes, so the wipe runs and still leaves
  sums of the message schedule where they lay. Every digest is right.
  bin/sha2_equiv_test measures how far below its caller the kernel writes
  and requires that, and 16 bytes more for a caller at another stack
  address, inside the length, and then requires no word a call computed
  in the stack below it. The kernel has a body on x86-64 alone, so the catch is the script,
  which builds the binary for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64, whose
  max model has AVX2 on every host. The lane skips without docker, and
  this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
#define SHA512_AVX2_BELOW_LEN 512
--- new
#define SHA512_AVX2_BELOW_LEN 192
